"""Autoconf substitutions for bash 5.2.37 on x86_64 Debian trixie (glibc).

Stands in for ./configure, which probes the host compiler and libc. Values are
what autoconf resolves for this target triple with the flags debian/rules
passes (--enable-largefile --without-bash-malloc --with-installed-readline),
plus SONiC's plugin patch, whose BASH_SHELL_EXECVE_PLUGIN entry is what makes
bash-tacplus loadable.

Verified byte-identical to a real configure run apart from the banner comment.
"""

# `#undef NAME` lines in config.h.in that configure turns into `#define`.
# Anything absent stays #undef. An empty value emits a bare `#define NAME`.
#
# USING_BASH_MALLOC is deliberately NOT here: debian/rules passes
# --without-bash-malloc, so bash uses glibc's allocator and lib/malloc/ is not
# built. (Verified: Make's deb contains none of lib/malloc's diagnostic
# strings.) The stale tree under src/bash/bash-5.2.37/ has it enabled because
